    "fileId": 23929,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Salivary duct carcinoma ex pleomorphic adenoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "An infiltrative mass involving the parotid gland, surrounding blood vessels and excretory ducts. In the upper-left corner there is an encapsulated cystic hyalinized hypocellular nodule (burnt-out pleomorphic adenoma) outlined by apocrine cells with a micropapillary architecture. Otherwise, the predominant growth pattern is solid. Foci of necrosis are common. Cytologically, neoplastic cells show amphophilic cytoplasm and pleomorphic nuclei with coarse chromatin and prominent nucleoli.",
    "source": "Simon Chiosea",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/23929.dzi",
    "thumbnail": null
